            <div xml:id="d284">

                <pb facs="0685" n="571" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg571"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 European War 1939/1567: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-08">August 8, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4815. My Greek colleague<anchor n="1" xml:id="d284-f1"/> tells me that the Papal
                        Nuncio<anchor n="2" xml:id="d284-f2"/> called upon him and asked him to pass
                    on to me and to my British colleague<anchor n="3" xml:id="d284-f3"/> the
                    following as coming from an Italian source here without revealing <pb
                        facs="0686" n="572" xml:id="pg572"/> his name: the Badoglio Government is
                    prepared to accept immediately armistice on “honorable terms” provided Italy is
                    not occupied. This only way for B to get Germans out. If Germans refuse B will
                    ask Allied assistance.</p>
                <p>My Greek colleague suggests action of Nuncio may well have been inspired by the
                    Vatican. Am inclined believe <hi rendition="#italic">Nonce</hi> acted on his own
                    initiative.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
